<!--
  MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.StructureSystems
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbt="com.machineblocks.bml.type">

  <name>StructureSystems</name>
  <type>concept:StructureSystems</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks structure systems</is>

  <documentation>
    Structure parameters add physical function inside the same bounding box that size defines.
    Geometry shapes the volume; structure makes it printable and connectable.

    Four structure systems:

    1. Body — base toggles the solid body. base=false hides the body while bounding box and
       alignment stay unchanged (useful for composite wrappers and stud-only layers).
    2. Underside — baseCutoutType selects None / Standard / Studs / Groove (enum member ids).
       baseWallGaps (WallGap[]) open passages through underside walls for crossing geometry.
    3. Enclosure — recess and recessWallThickness carve an interior; recessWallGaps
       (RecessWallGap[]) open walls. RecessWallGap extends WallGap with padStart / padEnd
       (default Auto) for tongue/groove-aware end insets. Do not use wall thickness 0 to create
       openings — use gaps.
    4. Connection — continuous tongue-and-groove versus discrete connectors for segmented or
       angled joints.

    Studs sit on the top grid. studBaseOverlap (mbu) sinks studs into the top surface; 0 is valid
    when base=false but studs still render.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:CompositionConcepts" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — composition, assembly, and parts.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:BaseCutout" relation="Defines">
      Underside cutout mode enum (None, Standard, Studs, Groove).
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:StudType" relation="Defines">
      Stud Solid / Hollow modes.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:WallGap" relation="Defines">
      Wall gap for underside openings (baseWallGaps) — face, pos, len.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:RecessWallGap" relation="Defines">
      Recess wall gap (recessWallGaps) — WallGap plus padStart / padEnd.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:Connector" relation="Defines">
      Discrete connector compound type.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="Defines">
      SSOT for base, studs, recess, tongue/groove, connectors, and related properties.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
